{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d53d7cfe-63b5-4ec1-bfbb-9352fdb8c0ca","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Updated [deploy.sh](file:///tmp/h-UVCv4q/scripts/deploy.sh#L12-L19) and documented the changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-UVCv4q/ANSWER.md):\n\n- **Per-extension `Content-Type` and `Cache-Control` loop**: Added the `aws s3 cp --recursive --metadata-directive REPLACE` loop after `aws s3 sync` so every file extension receives both an explicit `--content-type` and `--cache-control` together (preventing S3 from resetting `Content-Type` to `binary/octet-stream`):\n  - Short TTL (`public, max-age=300`) for `.html` (`text/html`), `.js` (`application/javascript`), and `.css` (`text/css`).\n  - Long TTL (`public, max-age=86400`) for `.png` (`image/png`) and `.svg` (`image/svg+xml`) in `assets/`.\n- **CloudFront invalidation**: Kept `aws cloudfront create-invalidation` after the metadata replacement loop so edge caches pick up the updated headers.\n","duration_seconds":145.829026,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":35488,"output_tokens":7189,"thinking_tokens":4857,"cache_read_tokens":102425,"total_tokens":42677}}}
